msgid ":mod:`!builtins` --- Built-in objects"
msgstr ":mod:`!builtins` --- inbyggda objekt"

msgid ""
"This module provides direct access to all 'built-in' identifiers of Python; "
"for example, ``builtins.open`` is the full name for the built-in function "
":func:`open`."
msgstr ""
"Den här modulen ger direkt åtkomst till alla Pythons inbyggda identifierare."
" ``builtins.open`` är till exempel det fullständiga namnet på den inbyggda "
"funktionen :func:`open`."

msgid ""
"This module is not normally accessed explicitly by most applications, but "
"can be useful in modules that provide objects with the same name as a built-"
"in value, but in which the built-in of that name is also needed.  For "
"example, in a module that wants to implement an :func:`open` function that "
"wraps the built-in :func:`open`, this module can be used directly::"
msgstr ""
"De flesta program använder normalt inte den här modulen direkt, men den kan "
"vara användbar i moduler som tillhandahåller objekt med samma namn som ett "
"inbyggt värde och samtidigt behöver det inbyggda värdet med det namnet. "
"Modulen kan till exempel användas direkt i en modul som vill implementera en"
" :func:`open`-funktion som omsluter den inbyggda :func:`open`-funktionen::"

msgid ""
"import builtins\n"
"\n"
"def open(path):\n"
"    f = builtins.open(path, 'r')\n"
"    return UpperCaser(f)\n"
"\n"
"class UpperCaser:\n"
"    '''Wrapper around a file that converts output to uppercase.'''\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, f):\n"
"        self._f = f\n"
"\n"
"    def read(self, count=-1):\n"
"        return self._f.read(count).upper()\n"
"\n"
"    # ..."
msgstr ""
"import builtins\n"
"\n"
"def open(path):\n"
"    f = builtins.open(path, 'r')\n"
"    return UpperCaser(f)\n"
"\n"
"class UpperCaser:\n"
"    '''Wrapper around a file that converts output to uppercase.'''\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self, f):\n"
"        self._f = f\n"
"\n"
"    def read(self, count=-1):\n"
"        return self._f.read(count).upper()\n"
"\n"
"    # ..."

msgid ""
"As an implementation detail, most modules have the name ``__builtins__`` "
"made available as part of their globals.  The value of ``__builtins__`` is "
"normally either this module or the value of this module's "
":attr:`~object.__dict__` attribute. Since this is an implementation detail, "
"it may not be used by alternate implementations of Python."
msgstr ""
"Som en implementeringsdetalj får de flesta moduler namnet ``__builtins__`` "
"tillgängligt som en del av sina globala variabler. Värdet för "
"``__builtins__`` är vanligen antingen den här modulen eller värdet av "
"modulens attribut :attr:`~object.__dict__`. Eftersom detta är en "
"implementeringsdetalj behöver den inte användas av alternativa Python-"
"implementationer."

